        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nPerfect! Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully extended the relay component to handle IPv6 addresses throughout the allocation and channel binding workflow. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**1. Updated `Allocation::can_relay_to()` method** (`rust/relay/src/server.rs:1028-1041`)\n   - Changed from a simple IPv4-only check to properly validate address family matching\n   - Now checks if the allocation supports the IP version of the peer address\n   - Returns `true` for IPv4 addresses when the allocation has an IPv4 relay address\n   - Returns `true` for IPv6 addresses when the allocation has an IPv6 relay address\n   - Properly handles dual-stack allocations (with both IPv4 and IPv6 relay addresses)\n\n**2. Added comprehensive tests** (`rust/relay/tests/regression.rs`)\n   - `can_bind_channel_to_ipv6_peer` - Tests ChannelBind success for IPv6 allocations\n   - `can_relay_data_to_ipv6_peer` - Tests full data relay workflow (client→peer and peer→client) for IPv6\n   - `ipv6_channel_bind_rejected_for_ipv4_allocation` - Tests that IPv6 peers are rejected for IPv4-only allocations\n   - `ipv4_channel_bind_rejected_for_ipv6_allocation` - Tests that IPv4 peers are rejected for IPv6-only allocations\n   - `can_bind_channel_to_ipv4_peer_with_dual_stack_allocation` - Tests IPv4 ChannelBind works with dual-stack\n   - `can_bind_channel_to_ipv6_peer_with_dual_stack_allocation` - Tests IPv6 ChannelBind works with dual-stack\n\n### How It Works\n\n1. **Allocation Phase**: When a client requests an IPv6 allocation, the server creates an allocation with an IPv6 relay address (already implemented in the existing codebase)\n\n2. **Channel Binding Phase**: When a client sends a ChannelBind request with an IPv6 peer address:\n   - The server calls `Allocation::can_relay_to()` to validate the peer address\n   - If the allocation supports IPv6, the binding succeeds\n   - If there's a version mismatch, the server returns `PeerAddressFamilyMismatch` error\n\n3. **Data Forwarding Phase**: \n   - **Client → Peer**: ChannelData messages are forwarded to the IPv6 peer using the allocated relay socket\n   - **Peer → Client**: UDP packets from IPv6 peers are encapsulated in ChannelData messages and sent back to the client on the bound channel\n\n4. **Address Family Matching**: The implementation correctly matches IP versions:\n   - IPv4 allocations can only bind to IPv4 peers\n   - IPv6 allocations can only bind to IPv6 peers\n   - Dual-stack allocations can bind to both IPv4 and IPv6 peers\n\nAll existing IPv4 allocation, binding, and data forwarding behavior remains unchanged and continues to pass their tests.",
